                                                "text": "armored personnel carrier"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6ad1d76-cc1a-48fb-8862-9b046fff58e8",
                                                "sense_id": "d3fce345-ec94-3a30-9c48-6f724618b042",
                                                "text": "The air which is but […] a carrier of the sounds."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e06cdeb-2261-3647-893f-0db9c1605c3c",
                                        "entry_id": "dc6a14de-d4d9-3342-99c9-c4663e255214",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person or object that carries someone or something else.",
                                            "Ellipsis of aircraft carrier."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74449eaa-e244-4c2b-8f42-f7bf98d04eb2",
                                                "sense_id": "7e06cdeb-2261-3647-893f-0db9c1605c3c",
                                                "text": "Two weeks later, I reported to Pensacola, Florida, for duty aboard CV-48, the USS Saipan, a boxy old carrier the Navy retired from fleet duty and reassigned for use in training."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e4d8932a-e993-35c0-a06f-312c68a7fe88",
                                        "entry_id": "dc6a14de-d4d9-3342-99c9-c4663e255214",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person or object that carries someone or something else.",
                                            "Ellipsis of aircraft carrier.",
                                            "A starship designed to carry starfighters"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a2d5433-72c4-459a-9007-1d790244d7f1",
                                                "sense_id": "e4d8932a-e993-35c0-a06f-312c68a7fe88",
                                                "text": "And each was hideously powerful: an attack carrier could destroy a world, a force of cruisers and spinship destroyers could destroy a sun."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f6777cd-92fb-4305-b222-a2a5a7f6acb6",
                                                "sense_id": "e4d8932a-e993-35c0-a06f-312c68a7fe88",
                                                "text": "The first carrier completely ignored us, sir! Blew through the Malta’s debris field and headed straight for Earth!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c75ffccb-aa0e-4bb1-a880-42a73e4672a5",
                                                "sense_id": "e4d8932a-e993-35c0-a06f-312c68a7fe88",
                                                "text": "In fleet combat, carriers stay clear of battle, launching fighters bearing disruptor torpedoes. Fighters are the primary striking power of the ship; if a carrier enters mass accelerator range of the enemy, things have gone very wrong.\nIt is possible to recover and rearm fighters during combat, though most carriers seal the flight deck and try to stay out of the way. The flight deck is essentially a corridor through the armor and into the heart of the vessel. A single well-placed torpedo is enough to gut a carrier.\nAlliance carriers are named after great leaders, artists, and intellectuals from human history."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "de53755c-a901-3fc1-b12e-03f9acdd49f1",
                                        "entry_id": "dc6a14de-d4d9-3342-99c9-c4663e255214",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person or object that carries someone or something else.",
                                            "Ellipsis of carrier bag."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "86c18268-3921-38ad-ab10-8614cb2dbd92",
                                        "entry_id": "dc6a14de-d4d9-3342-99c9-c4663e255214",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A carrier pigeon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae550916-0c65-36c1-bdae-1b0f2eff7d51",
                                        "entry_id": "dc6a14de-d4d9-3342-99c9-c4663e255214",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person or company in the business of shipping freight."
                                        ],
